<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Split Sheet Studio Windows Plugin | VST3 Download</title>
  <meta name="description" content="Download the Split Sheet Studio Windows VST3 plugin and standalone Windows app for DAW-based split sheets, remote signatures, and final PDF delivery.">
  <link rel="canonical" href="https://splitsheetstudio.com/plugin"><meta name="theme-color" content="#171311">
  <meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:title" content="Split Sheet Studio Windows Plugin | VST3 Download"><meta property="og:description" content="Download the Windows VST3 plugin and standalone app for DAW-based music split sheets, remote signatures, and final PDF delivery."><meta property="og:url" content="https://splitsheetstudio.com/plugin"><meta property="og:image" content="<%= socialImageUrl %>">
  <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta name="twitter:title" content="Split Sheet Studio Windows VST3 Plugin"><meta name="twitter:description" content="Create music split sheets directly inside compatible Windows VST3 DAWs."><meta name="twitter:image" content="<%= socialImageUrl %>">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/premium.css">
</head>
<body class="premium-site"><div class="premium-shell">
  <%- include('partials/site-nav') %>
  <main class="store-page">
    <section class="store-hero premium-container">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-dot"></span> Windows VST3 · Version <%= pluginVersionLabel %></div>
        <h1>Get Split Sheet Studio<br><span>inside your DAW.</span></h1>
        <p class="hero-lede">Install the Windows plugin, sign in with your hosted account, create a split sheet, send remote signature links, and confirm the final PDF delivery.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="premium-button premium-button-primary" href="#windows-download">Download plugin</a>
          <a class="premium-button premium-button-ghost" href="<%= appUrl %>/signup">Create account</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <aside class="purchase-card">
        <div class="purchase-label">WINDOWS DOWNLOAD</div>
        <h2>VST3 plugin + standalone app</h2>
        <p>Built for compatible 64-bit Windows DAWs, with the standalone Windows app included for sessions outside the DAW.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Installs VST3 to the standard Windows folder</li>
          <li>Installs standalone app for quick access</li>
          <li>Connects to <%= appUrl %></li>
          <li>Checks for updates on plugin open</li>
        </ul>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section id="windows-download" class="premium-section premium-container included-section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div><div class="section-kicker">Install checklist</div><h2>Run this sequence for a clean Windows DAW setup.</h2></div>
        <p>Close your DAW before installing because audio hosts can lock the VST3 file while it is loaded.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-list-grid">
        <div><span>01</span><h3>Download</h3><p>Use the Windows installer link on this page. If Windows SmartScreen appears, choose More info only if you trust this installer source.</p></div>
        <div><span>02</span><h3>Install</h3><p>Run the installer. It places the plugin in <code>C:\Program Files\Common Files\VST3</code> and adds the standalone app.</p></div>
        <div><span>03</span><h3>Rescan</h3><p>Open your VST3-compatible Windows DAW, run its plug-in scan if needed, then search for “Split Sheet Studio” under effects.</p></div>
        <div><span>04</span><h3>Test</h3><p>Sign in, create a two-person split, send invite links, sign both links, and confirm both final emails arrive.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-actions centered"><a class="premium-button premium-button-primary" href="<%= installerUrl %>">Download Windows installer →</a></div>
    </section>

    <section class="premium-section requirements-section">
      <div class="premium-container requirements-grid">
        <div><div class="section-kicker">Compatibility checklist</div><h2>What to confirm inside your DAW.</h2></div>
        <ul class="premium-checks">
          <li><i>✓</i><span>Plugin opens in a compatible Windows VST3 host without the standalone app running</span></li>
          <li><i>✓</i><span>Login, create account, forgot password, and update buttons are visible</span></li>
          <li><i>✓</i><span>Writer and publisher totals must equal 100%</span></li>
          <li><i>✓</i><span>Remote collaborator links finalize only after every party signs</span></li>
          <li><i>✓</i><span>Completed email includes PDF download and revised split-sheet link</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="premium-section premium-container faq-section">
      <div class="section-kicker">Download notes</div>
      <h2>What to know before installing.</h2>
      <div class="faq-grid">
        <article><h3>Is the installer signed?</h3><p>The current Windows installer may show a Windows SmartScreen warning until code signing is completed. Only install from Split Sheet Studio links you trust.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Can I upgrade from my account?</h3><p>Yes. Creator and Studio checkout is available from the account Plans tab and the pricing page.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Do plugin updates auto-install?</h3><p>No. The plugin checks for updates and opens the download. The user closes the DAW and runs the installer.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Which DAWs are supported?</h3><p>The current download supports 64-bit Windows DAWs that host VST3 effects, including Studio One, Ableton Live, FL Studio, Cubase, Nuendo, REAPER, Bitwig Studio, Cakewalk Sonar, Mixcraft, Waveform, Reason, Samplitude, and Adobe Audition. Pro Tools requires AAX, and BandLab web/mobile do not host desktop VST3 plugins.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Where do I report issues?</h3><p>Email <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a> with your DAW, Windows version, and what happened.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <%- include('partials/site-footer') %>
</div></body></html>
